    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "CAREER LEARNING-ESL\nSteward-Stewardess Announcement\nGood morning Ladies and Gentlemen and welcome aboard Western\nAirlines, Flight #638 now departing non-stop to Mexico City. Our flight\ntime this morning will be approximately 3 and 1/2 hours.\nSince there is\na two hour difference in time, we are scheduled to land at 2:05 p.m.\nMexico City time.\nYour stewardesses serving you this morning are\nin the aft cabin and\nand myself in the forward\nand\ncabin.\nFor those of you who are not familiar with our Boeing 707 aircraft\nwe will now give a brief demonstration of our cabin safety features.\nIn\ncase of any rapid change in cabin pressure, an oxigen mask will be releas-\ned automatically from the compartment just above your seat. Before taking\nhold of the mask, please extinguish all cigarettes. Then pull the mask\ndown firmly, placing it over your nose and mouth, and continue to breathe\nnormally until advised by a crew member to discontinue its use.\nThere are six emergency exits on this aircraft. We have two doors\nin the aft cabin, one on either side of the aircraft and two doors in the\nforward cabin. Just over the wings we have two removable window exits.\nIt is a safety regulation that you put your chair back and tray\ntable in their original up-right positions. Please do not smoke until\nour captain has turned off the no-smoking sign.\nWe hope you have an enjoyable trip with us this morning. If there\nis anything we can do to make your trip more pleasant, please feel free\nto call on us.\nThank you"
    ],
